From 8745a78fa146eb3e8549ccbf76229f26d7463e94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:53:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 206/211] webui: fix static-DHCP client dropdown clipping (LAN
 > DHCP Server)

The Manually-Assigned-IP client picker (#ClientList_Block_PC) inherits the
stock .clientlist_dropdown rule (device-map.css: position:absolute +
height:auto + overflow-y:auto). height:auto defeats its own overflow, so the
full LAN client list grows past the framed page body; the shell frame sizes to
BODY height and an abspos overlay opening does not re-fire the fit, so the list
clips at the frame edge. Worst on the default page (empty static-lease table =
short body), which is why adding rows 'works around' it.

Same remedy as the v1.6.6b WAN DNS-list flyout (BUG C): re-anchor to the frame
viewport (position:fixed, centered) with a real inner scroll (max-height:88vh).
Scoped via :has(input[name=dhcp_staticmac_x_0]) to THIS page's unique
static-lease MAC input - the ~20 other pages sharing the id keep stock
anchoring (short lists, no clip); a browser without :has() just keeps today's
behavior. reaper_content.css only, no logic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css  | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
index ceb881af02..b34b2a37f2 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
+++ b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
@@ -793,6 +793,25 @@ body.bg,.container.no_highlights,.content_container{background:transparent!impor
   transform:translate(-50%,-50%)!important;
   max-height:88vh!important;overflow-y:auto!important}
 
+/* BACKLOG 2026-07-22 (owner-reported): static-DHCP client picker. On LAN > DHCP
+   Server the Manually-Assigned-IP client dropdown (#ClientList_Block_PC) inherits
+   .clientlist_dropdown (device-map.css:990): position:absolute + height:auto +
+   overflow-y:auto - height:auto defeats its own overflow (same defect class as
+   BUG C above), so the full LAN client list grows past the page body. The shell
+   frame auto-sizes to BODY height only (an abspos overlay opening does not
+   re-fire the fit), so the list clips at the frame edge; the default page (empty
+   static-lease table = short body) is the worst case, which is why adding rows
+   "works around" it. Same remedy as BUG C: re-anchor to the frame viewport with
+   a real inner scroll. Scoped via :has() to this page's unique static-lease MAC
+   input because ~20 other pages share the id and keep their stock anchoring
+   (short lists, no clip); a browser without :has() just keeps today's behavior. */
+body:has(input[name="dhcp_staticmac_x_0"]) #ClientList_Block_PC.clientlist_dropdown{
+  position:fixed!important;
+  top:50%!important;left:50%!important;
+  margin:0!important;
+  transform:translate(-50%,-50%)!important;
+  max-height:88vh!important;overflow-y:auto!important}
+
 /* BUG D: Network Map status iframe (#statusframe) is pinned to 760px but the inner
    clients.asp document (client rows + tall NM min-heights) is taller and has no inner
    scroll region, so the iframe's own scrollbar stacks against the page scrollbar = a
